asof:"Daily scan 23 Nov 2026 (08:50 SGT). Prices: no US session since Fri 20 Nov (weekend); latest close unchanged — GOOG $264.00, −2.59%; GOOGL $265.29, −2.70% (Nasdaq.com quote API shows 20 Nov as last trade, checked 23 Nov 08:45 SGT). Day range 20 Nov GOOG $262.28–$280.52 / GOOGL $264.22–$283.14; GOOG's $262.28 intraday low is the new 52-week low (Nasdaq.com 52-week field still $270.72–$404.47 GOOG / $272.11–$408.61 GOOGL). After-hours 20 Nov 7:59pm ET (stockanalysis): GOOG $268.50 (+1.70%). Weekly (Longbridge recap, 21 Nov): GOOG −9.75%, GOOGL −10.31% for the week. Financials: through Q3 2026 (10-Q filed 29 Oct 2026). CapEx: no change in management guidance vs 21 Nov: 2026 $195–205bn (reaffirmed 28 Oct); 2027 to increase significantly, details on the Q4 call. Not guidance: President Trump said on 20 Nov that US companies building data centres abroad will face a 'tremendous tax' (no rate, legal authority or plan given; CNBC/Politico) — policy risk for Google's overseas builds (e.g. $15bn Malaysia 2027–28), not a capex figure; a third-party summary of Bloomberg's 22 Nov 'Leaders' interview with Ruth Porat cites ~$280bn 2027 capex — appears to be Bloomberg/Street framing, not a management figure (unverified; captions blocked). Street: UBS 2027 capex estimate $340bn (17 Nov; broker estimate). SEC: no new filings since the 20 Nov FWP and 8-A12B (EDGAR submissions checked 23 Nov 08:45 SGT); no 8-K, 10-Q, Form 4, Form 144, 13F or 424B. C$6.0bn notes settle 24 Nov. Analysts: no new rating/PT changes found 21–23 Nov. S&P Global mean PT $397.13 unchanged (median $390.69; 58 analysts, 43/10/5/0); fwd P/E 18.74 (stockanalysis statistics, updated 22 Nov; was 19.14 — same price, estimate basis moved); market cap $3.25tn, EV $3.16tn. Legal/regulatory: YouTube reached an agreement in principle to pay ~$3bn to thousands of US school districts over addiction claims (Bloomberg via Reuters, 20 Nov; needs majority sign-on and approval by Judge Gonzalez Rogers; Google declined comment); publisher ad tech antitrust trial (S.D.N.Y. MDL, Judge Castel) moved to 25 Oct 2027 from 5 Apr 2027 at Google's request (MLex/Law360, 19 Nov); Search appeal (D.C. Cir.) is calendared for the first appropriate date in January 2027 per the court's 9 Oct order (eCorpIT / Newzino; exact day not public) — earlier '9 Dec earliest' catalyst corrected; Indonesia's digital ministry asked Google to explain the removal of 19,389 YouTube channels (Antara/Straits Times, 20 Nov). People: Sundar Pichai on X (20 Nov) on the claimed Riemann Hypothesis proofs: 'Somewhere Euler, Gauss and Riemann in awe today!'; Ruth Porat (President & CIO) on Bloomberg Leaders (22 Nov) on AI investment discipline, data-centre backlash and US-first infrastructure. Waymo: Miami police cruiser pushed into a stopped Waymo in Little Havana after another car hit it (22 Nov; rider taken to hospital; Miami Herald); freeway pause continues in all markets (Fox Business, 21 Nov). Products: no new Google blog posts since 20 Nov; AI Mode desktop sidebar rolling out globally (Robby Stein; India Today 22 Nov). Video: 1 new (Bloomberg Originals, Leaders with Francine Lacqua: Ruth Porat, 22 Nov); one 8 Oct item aged out of the 45-day window. 15 Nov items rolled off. SGT",
